{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459627-werewolf-and-recent-events","id":1459627,"title":"Werewolf and Recent events.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-10T23:48:06-07:00","id":1459627,"title":"Werewolf and Recent events.","content":"Do you think recent events would alter the garou perception of their fight against the wyrm?<br /> <br /> A sickness spread through the entire world, effectively upsetting the industrial order of the weaver so much that it had to shut down temporarily and cast the looming shadow of the wyrm over the world as it struggled to deal with the crisis at hand. This was Also the greatest time of growth and healing nature had ever experienced since the birth of the industrial era. A record-breaking series of ecological bounce-backs happened simultaneously across the global the moment the weaver retreated and humanity stopped poisoning gaia for five seconds.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't this raise a lot of questions in the garou community about whether they're even fighting the right enemy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T08:31:08-07:00","id":1459655,"title":"","content":"I think that for the smart werewolves, this is more just a confirmation of what they knew already. The vast majority of the disaster they face is done by a relatively small number of people and organizations. Should they have access to wrecking through those institutions, they happily would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T08:54:57-07:00","id":1459661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459627-werewolf-and-recent-events?p=1459655#post1459655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that for the smart werewolves, this is more just a confirmation of what they knew already. The vast majority of the disaster they face is done by a relatively small number of people and organizations. Should they have access to wrecking through those institutions, they happily would.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much that. Even Weaver-focused Garou know who are responsible for the major ecological threats.<br /> <br /> Most would just interpret those events as proving their points. Human-haters point out that killing humans is working, technology-lovers point out that high technology will save us, tradition-defenders point out that everything would be better if we all followed old traditions... business as usual in the Garou Nation.<br /> <br /> You can use the recent events as basis to determine that other things are happening in the setting. But by themselves those events aren't really that spectacular for the Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T13:39:46-07:00","id":1459690,"title":"","content":"Also, the Garou can talk to their ancestors, who have seen this before. It's a cycle that's been going on for a long, long time. A natural disaster of a large scale happens (diseases of course being some of the largest scale in that regard). For a brief moment, it looks like humanity has a chance to change course. But then it's gone as fear drives us to vilify each other and focus more on fighting than fixing, and drives humans to further pray that technology will save us from ourselves. And we do it all over again the next time. This is the stuff of Garou Harano, not celebration.<br /> <br /> The Garou are going to look at smaller stories, like humans started to accept that reintroducing wild wolves to an area is actually really good for everybody, for hope that change is possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T20:00:09-07:00","id":1459715,"title":"","content":"*The Ratkin Plague Lords pouting in the corner bout not getting any of the credit.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}